{"id":"n1-197","title":"～ところを","romaji":"〜tokoro wo","jlptLevel":1,"shortExplanation":"Indicates a contrasting or inconvenient timing; 'just when...', 'even though...'.","longExplanation":"The grammar point ～ところを is often used when something happens (or one acts) at a certain moment/condition that makes the timing inconvenient or contrary to what is expected. It can imply “in spite of the fact that...” or “just when...” depending on context.","formation":"Verb-ている + ところを / Noun + の + ところを / い-Adjective + ところを / な-Adjective + な + ところを","examples":[{"jp":"ちょうど映画を見ているところを、停電で真っ暗になった。","romaji":"Choudo eiga o mite iru tokoro o, teiden de makkura ni natta.","en":"Just when I was in the middle of watching a movie, the power went out and everything went dark.","words":[{"surface":"ちょうど","vocabId":"1427340","reading":"ちょうど"},{"surface":"映画","vocabId":"1173720","reading":"えいが"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"見","vocabId":"1259290","reading":"みる","baseForm":"見る"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いる","vocabId":"1577980","reading":"いる"},{"surface":"ところ","vocabId":"1343100","reading":"ところ"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"停電","vocabId":"1435020","reading":"ていでん"},{"surface":"で","vocabId":null},{"surface":"真っ暗","vocabId":"1363190","reading":"まっくら"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"なっ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"なる"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[4,5,6,7]},{"jp":"美味しく食べているところを、彼が全部横取りしてしまった。","romaji":"Oishiku tabete iru tokoro o, kare ga zenbu yokodori shite shimatta.","en":"Right when I was enjoying my meal, he took it all away.","words":[{"surface":"美味しく","vocabId":"1486650","reading":"おいしい","baseForm":"美味しい"},{"surface":"食べ","vocabId":"1358280","reading":"たべる","baseForm":"食べる"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いる","vocabId":"1577980","reading":"いる"},{"surface":"ところ","vocabId":"1343100","reading":"ところ"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surfa